=== PACKET SECTION (technique catalogue, Packet #12 / style-library §T212) ===
T212 — Margin bar field (every state a bar, margin as dotted extension) (P12 T11) — OWED #99. Mechanics: all states become vertical bars in winner colour; above each solid bar, a dotted column extension shows the losing side's share — "no state is actually all-red or all-blue" (transcript 2:36). Operation: bar growth + dotted extension; the margin is drawn, per state, before any allocation is discussed. The film's honesty device: the margin is made visible as physical stuff first, so its erasure in T214 is something the viewer has seen. Feeds: diagram · transition — P12 @ 2:37–2:52 — ev/t162-margin-bars.jpg · clips/t10-margin-bars.mp4. (Binding priced reading from the wave record's Observe, fed per jev-prewave §3: the lifecycle is two forms — the STACKED share field (blue/grey/red per bar, majority line, rotated labels) holds first, yellow annotation arcs draw, the field flattens to winner colour, shrinks to an equal solid strip, then dotted winner-colour extensions grow per state with heights tracking losing-side VOLUME via per-state loserUnits (VISUAL ESTIMATES, CA=100); the dotted hold runs to window end; the Minnesota card overlaying the tail from ~171.5 s is T213, a separate technique, deferred by name.)

